# Testing and Quality Baseline

## Quality gates

- At minimum, run `lint` for all code changes.
- For risky changes (auth, booking flow, data writes), also run build/type checks.
- Do not mark task complete if checks fail due to new issues.

## Test expectations

- For new business logic, add automated tests when test infra exists.
- If tests are not yet set up, include a concrete manual verification checklist in PR/summary.
- Prioritize coverage for critical flows: login/signup, booking creation, dashboard data loading.

## Security and config hygiene

- Never hardcode secrets or Supabase keys in source files.
- Keep env usage documented and consistent with runtime needs.
- Validate and sanitize user-provided input before DB writes.
